-- Add hazard videos to Lesson 4: Hazard Recognition
UPDATE lessons
SET 
  content_data = jsonb_build_object(
    'content', (content_data->>'content') || E'\n\n---\n\n## Training Videos: See the Hazards in Action\n\n### Powered Haulage: Understanding Blind Spots\n\n**VIDEO: Truck Blind Spot Demonstration**\nURL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_d1Y__h5BSQ\n*Cue: "Now let''s see what that haul truck''s driver can—and more importantly, can''t—see from the cab."*\n\nThis powerful visual demonstration shows how a full-size pickup truck can completely disappear from a haul truck driver''s view. Never assume an operator sees you.\n\n### Machinery & Lockout/Tagout (LOTO)\n\n**VIDEO: Lockout/Tagout Procedure for Safety**\nURL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-DIod50ZEu4\n*Cue: "Reaching into a machine is a fatal mistake. The only way to work safely is to control the energy. Let''s watch a proper Lockout/Tagout procedure."*\n\nThis step-by-step demonstration teaches a critical, life-saving skill. Video is vastly superior to text for learning this complex, sequential procedure.\n\n### Ground Control: Inspecting Highwalls\n\n**VIDEO: MSHA - Inspecting Highwalls for Signs of Failure**\nURL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=G5HnPX6cBeQ\n*Cue: "The ground was telling that miner something important. This MSHA video shows us exactly what to look for when examining a highwall for signs of failure."*\n\nLearn to spot specific hazards like tension cracks and other warning signs of ground failure.\n\n### Ground Control: Stockpile Hazards\n\n**VIDEO: Hazards of Coal Stockpiling Operations**\nURL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hw7ruTSZwXM\n*Cue: "Undercutting a stockpile creates a deadly engulfment hazard. This MSHA video uses a model to show you why this is so dangerous and how quickly it can happen."*\n\n### Health Hazards: Respirable Silica Dust\n\n**VIDEO: What is Silica Dust?**\nURL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=N5Tyhii-FaM\n*Cue: "One of the biggest long-term health risks you''ll face is invisible. This video explains what respirable silica dust is and how we control it."*\n\nSee the dust control methods like water sprays that protect your long-term health.'
  )
WHERE id = '5b661df6-0187-4611-8831-e8101c27eff2';